{
 "summary": [
  "A project chat gets six control tools that do what the user's buttons do: approve_plan, start_work, start_step, restart_review, message_agent, stop_agent",
  "Approve logic moves from the IPC handler in index.ts into Orchestrator.approve, shared by the button and the chat tool",
  "Orchestrator gains agentOf (which session a message goes to) and stopAgents (stop all running agents of a work/step)",
  "ToolActions grows seven actions wired in index.ts to orchestrator methods; tools.ts routes the new tools to controlTool, which checks the caller is a project chat and logs each action",
  "ProjectEvent kind 'chat' added for the log of chat-driven actions; chat prompt and tool descriptions say to act only on the user's explicit request"
 ],
